 becomes softer or loses its original shape, lower the drying temperature. In the case of loss of transparency, use a different device. The spool can’t be put into the environment without a controlled value of relative humidity after drying. The cooling process must be taken in the desiccator (or in the sealing box with the content of silica gel). If the hot spool is placed into an environment with higher humidity, the moisture may be absorbed back in about 10 minutes. And possibly on a higher level of moisture than it was before drying! The coil should not be left in the dryer after it has been switched off, as there is still evaporated moisture in the environment which can be absorbed back into the filament in the same way."}]},{"id":"P1027","product":"G090-03","source":"R-COLORFABB-TDS-colorFabb-XT-CF20","kind":"Manufacturer published guidance","at":"p. 2: Recommended printing settings","nozzle":{"text":"240-260 °C","state":"range","requirement":"required","min":240,"max":260,"verdict":"within"},"bed":{"text":"60-70 °C","state":"range","requirement":"required","min":60,"max":70,"verdict":"within"},"chamber":{"state":"unknown","verdict":"unknown"},"notes":[{"topic":"Cooling","text":"0 %"},{"topic":"Speed","text":"40-70 mm/s"}]},{"id":"P1662","product":"G090-03","source":"R-COLORFABB-PRINT-20260928-889899362b76","kind":"Manufacturer published guidance","at":"p. 1: Advised 3D printing temperature; p. 1: Advised Heated bed","nozzle":{"text":"240-260C","state":"range","requirement":"required","min":240,"max":260,"verdict":"within"},"bed":{"text":"60-70C","state":"range","requirement":"required","min":60,"max":70,"verdict":"within"},"chamber":{"state":"unknown","verdict":"unknown"},"abrasion":"We recommend to use from stainless steel nozzles or nozzles made with hardened copper alloys.","advice":"harder-than-brass","replaced":["nozzle","bed"]},{"id":"P1935","product":"G090-03","source":"R-COLORFABB-PRINT-20260928-e02f420a2e56","kind":"Manufacturer published guidance","